# Vantage Movers Server Organization

- `vantage-main-server` is the Vercel-hosted Express REST API. Production: `https://vantage-movers-main-server.vercel.app`.
- Runtime code: `src/`. Tooling: `scripts/`. Architecture/schema notes: `docs/`.
- Before changing write paths, identify `TEST_MODE`, selected Mongo DB, target Google Sheet env vars, and whether the code can touch CRM, Postman, Twilio, Drive, or production customer data.

## API Launch Map

- **Entry:** `api/index.ts` re-exports `src/app.ts` (Express bootstrap, CORS, JSON 5mb, health/db, route mounts).
- **Local dev:** `scripts/dev-server.ts` (`pnpm dev` / `dev:local` / `dev:granot`).
- `src/routes/` owns HTTP boundaries — keep thin: auth → Zod → service → response.
- `src/routes/v1.routes.ts` is the main surface (public v1 + admin browse/search/export/analytics/registry/observability + extension workflows). Mounted after most cron/webhook routes.
- Before the `/api/v1` guard inside v1: `extension-auth.routes.ts` (`/api/v1/extension/auth/*`, no secret) and `google-drive-oauth.routes.ts` (mounted **inside** `v1.routes.ts`, not a separate `app.use`). OAuth callback is unguarded; other `/api/v1/admin/google-drive/*` routes attach per-route `requireApiSecret` + owner gate.
- After the guard: `ringcentral-registry.routes.ts` (`/api/v1/admin/ringcentral/inbound-routes*`) and `granot-lifecycle-admin.routes.ts` (`/api/v1/admin/granot-lifecycle/*`).
- Separate admin routers mounted from `src/app.ts` (still under `/api/v1/admin/...`, with `requireApiSecret`):
  - `granot-automation.routes.ts` — Granot HTTP automation (mounted **before** v1)
  - `ingestion.routes.ts` — Best Relocation ingestion (after v1)
  - `reporting.routes.ts` — reporting definitions/destinations/runs (after v1)
- Cron/webhook mounts from `src/app.ts` (before v1): RC webhooks (`/api/webhooks/ringcentral`, `/api/webhooks/ringcentral-local`, `/api/dev/ringcentral/*`), Granot webhooks (`/api/webhooks/granot/{lead-created,priority-updated,booking-status-changed}`), RC crons (`ringcentral-call-log-sync`, `ringcentral-analytics-reconcile`), booking-reconciliation rematch, sheet-sync drain, lead-messaging drain, CPL-corrections drain, notification digest, Twilio status/voice, Best Relocation ingest heartbeat, reporting crons (`reporting-delivery-heartbeat`, `reporting-health-scan`, `reporting-cleanup-janitor`, `reporting-test-artifact-janitor`), Granot automation heartbeat, Granot lifecycle drain (`/api/cron/granot-lifecycle-drain`).
- `app.ts` also calls `registerReportingStage4Foundation()` at Express bootstrap. Queue consumers do not inherit this — they must re-register foundations themselves.
- **Queue consumers** (`api/queues/`): `sheet-sync-consumer`, `lead-messaging-consumer`, `best-relocation-ingestion-consumer`, `reporting-consumer`, `granot-automation-consumer`, `granot-lifecycle-consumer` (`granot-lifecycle-events*`, `{ receipt_id }` only). Mongo remains the durable work source; the consumer is a wake-up.
- `src/validation/` — Zod schemas (`v1.validation.ts` barrel + `src/validation/v1/` + reporting validators).
- `src/models/` — runtime Mongoose schemas (`snake_case`); Google Sheets projections produce Title Case columns. `GranotObservationReceipt` lives here; collection `granot_webhook_receipts` is retained. `GranotObservation` lives here; collection `granot_observations`. `SynchronizationDecision`, `GranotLifecycleActivation`, and `GranotRecordLink` are Unit 07 evidence/current-state models.
- `src/config/domain/` — mode-aware domain config; re-exported by `src/config/domain.ts` **except** `reporting.ts` (import `./domain/reporting` directly). Prefer focused modules over scattering `process.env`. `granotLifecycle.ts` owns the ten centralized lifecycle flags (processing/shadow default true; all eight effect flags stay false).
- `src/db.ts` — shared Mongo helper; preserve `TEST_MODE` DB boundary.
- `src/middleware/` — `requireApiSecret` / `requireVantageAuth`, `requireGranotWebhookSecret`, HTTP logging.
- `src/auth/extension/` — Granot extension login, JWT, password hashing, `ExtensionUser`.

## Auth Surface

| Mechanism | Scope |
|-----------|--------|
| `x-api-secret` → extension Bearer (owner only on data routes; employees 403) → scoped keys (`VANTAGE_SCOPED_API_KEYS`) | Protected `/api/v1/*` after extension mount. Sets `req.vantageAuth`: `secret` \| `scoped_key` \| `user`. Scoped keys may also constrain Source Company + Source Granularity. |
| Extension auth (unguarded) | `/api/v1/extension/auth/{login,refresh,me,logout}` |
| Admin proxy actors | Trusted `x-vantage-admin-*` (+ optional HMAC). Registry/source/CPL/RC/ingestion/granot/booking-recon owner gates use `requireRegistry*Actor` patterns |
| Google Drive owner gate | Drive OAuth/Picker admin routes |
| Employee booking | Secret-only; submit also needs `x-public-client-key-hash` |
| Cron | Bearer or `x-cron-secret` |
| Granot / Twilio / RingCentral webhooks | Their own secret/signature validators |

Do not bypass the v1 auth guard for new data endpoints.

## Services by Domain

Prefer `src/services/<domain>/` imports over legacy barrels (`v1.service.ts`, `*Search.service.ts`, enrichment/reconciliation/crm/googleSheets top-level barrels).

### Core
- `leads/` — Form/call CRUD, duplicates, source match, location enrichment, CPL snapshot via `leadCplResolution.ts`, trusted Ingestion Origin + immutable ingested snapshots via `leadIngestionProvenance.ts`. Models: `FormLead`, `CallLead`
- `leadSourceCompanies/` — legacy embedded source-company document helpers and CPL reads; admin writes go through `operationsRegistry/`. Lead write paths still call this via `leads/leadSourceCompany.ts`.
- `bookings/` — Booked CRUD, from-source, referral/leadless, mirrors. Model: `BookedLead`
- `cancellations/` — Cancelled CRUD + sheet mirrors. Model: `CancelledLead`
- `customers/` — Customer CRUD/upsert. Model: `Customer`
- `agents/` — Receiver-agent CRM username attribution. Model: `Agent`
- `catalog/` — Admin agents/merchants catalog
- `cpl/` — CPL rate reads (schedules/corrections live in ops registry)
- `testimonials/`, `movingCarriers/` — Testimonials + carrier admin
- `search/` — Extension browse/search for form/call leads
- `errors/` — `AppError`, codes, registry error shapes

### Extension & Granot
- `enrichment/` — Call-lead enrichment preview/sync from Granot Follow Up rows
- `reconciliation/` — Booked call-lead reconciliation from Granot Booked Jobs rows
- `granotCrmCsv/` — CSV source registry + S3 ingest (`/granot-crm/csv/*`)
- `granotWebhooks/` — Compatibility adapter only; webhook capture implementation lives in `granotLifecycle/capture`
- `granotHttpCollector/` — HTTP session collector + automation runs/sources/workflows. Approved apply captures `granot_http_automation` receipts and enters `claimAndProcessOrPoll`. Preview matching stays guidance-only. See `businesslogic/granotHttpCollector.service.md`.
- `granotLifecycle/` — Shared lifecycle vocabulary, receipt evidence helpers, webhook capture, channel-neutral operation-ID capture, Owner extension apply (`extensionApply.ts`), HTTP automation apply (`automationApply.ts`), receipt-ID queue wake-up publisher, callable Observation normalization (`normalization.ts`), fail-closed source-policy/gate evaluation (`sourcePolicy.ts`), read-only source-scoped identity (`identity.ts`), desired-state planner (`leadDesiredState.ts`, `granotTemporal.ts`), channel-neutral shadow processor (`processor.ts`, `operations.ts`, `projections.ts`), the Unit 08 claim/drainer (`drainer.ts`), the Unit 09 revision CAS primitive (`aggregateRevision.ts`), and Unit 12 trusted Granot create validators (`trustedLeadCreateValidation.ts`, capability only — no live caller). Webhook capture still does not invoke the processor; extension and automation apply capture then call `claimAndProcessOrPoll`. The processor consumes identity and the planner; production Lead writes/creation/cases stay false. Queue/cron/requeue enter the same fenced claim service. Form/Call documents store immutable Ingestion Origin and ingested snapshots. Historical rows receive fail-closed `legacy_unknown` / `legacy_baseline` only through `scripts/migrations/granot-lifecycle-lead-provenance.ts`; the seven non-unique Lead S08 indexes are applied by `scripts/migrations/granot-lifecycle-indexes.ts`. Effect/creation flags stay false.
- `crm/` — Outbound Granot form-lead submit (invoked from lead write paths). Independent of webhook capture.

### Integrations
- `googleSheets/` + `sheetSync/` — Sheets client/projections + write-behind outbox/drainer/queue
- `googleAuth/` — Service-account credential loading
- `googleDriveOAuth/` — Owner OAuth connection, picker, folders, managed tabs, token encryption
- `googleMaps/` — Geocoding health
- `leadMessaging/` — Twilio SMS confirmation + voice helpers + queue
- `operationalWorkbooks/` — Registered operational spreadsheet IDs/masks

### RingCentral
- Routes are HTTP/cron boundaries only. Logic lives in `ringcentral/`: auth/client, webhook capture, candidates, Call Log sync, analytics reconcile, duplicate detection, call-lead ingest.
- Operations Registry inbound-route snapshot owns runtime inbound-number → source attribution. `call-lead-sources.ts` is migration/test seed only — do not import it at runtime. `ringcentral-call-lead-ingest.service.ts` is the shared promotion path — do not create RC call leads from routes/scripts directly.
- `ringcentral-config.ts` is the single source for RC env toggles and write posture.

### Admin / analytics / observability / registry
- `admin/` — Scope (`production|historical|combined`), browse/detail/export, search/facets, sheet-sync admin
- `analytics/` — Summary/trends/funnels + overview + agent-sales
- `observability/` — Events, incidents, notifications, operational reports
- `operationsRegistry/` — Agents/merchants/sources/granularities/CPL schedules+corrections/RC inbound routes + Granot CRM source lifecycle Registry commands + change audit

### Reporting / ingestion / automation / durable
- `reporting/` — Definitions, revisions, previews, runs, deliveries, destinations; Google adapters; queue worker; live harness/janitor
- `ingestion/` — Best Relocation connection/runs/conflicts/queue worker
- `bestRelocationSheetIngest/` — Sheet inspect/plan/apply for BR ingest
- `employeeBookings/` — Public employee booking submit + admin booking-lead reconciliation cases
- `domainCommands/` — Transaction-owning canonical command executor + existing write adapters + append-only `EntityChange`. See [`domainCommands.service.md`](../businesslogic/domainCommands.service.md). Later lifecycle/owner commands remain disabled.
- `durableWork/` — Leases, checksums, actors, checkpoints for long-running jobs
- `historicalConsolidation/` — Staged historical→production merge helpers

## Admin Route Groups (`/api/v1/admin`)

- **Discovery:** `search`, `facets`
- **Catalog/people:** `catalog/agents|merchants`, `agents`, `merchants` (+ activation/dependencies)
- **Sources/CPL:** `source-companies`, `source-granularities`, `source-resolution/preview`, `cpl-rates`, `cpl/snapshot|simple-schedule`, CPL periods/commands, `cpl-corrections*`
- **Browse + CSV:** `form-leads`, `call-leads`, `booked-leads`, `cancelled-leads`, `customers`, `agents` (+ `exports/{resource}.csv`)
- **Analytics/reports:** `analytics/*` (incl. `overview`, `receiver-agent-*`), `exports/analytics/:report.csv`, `exports/reports/agent-sales.csv`, `reports/agent-sales`
- **Ops tooling:** `sheet-sync/*`, `google-maps/geocoding-health`, `lead-messages/*`, `testimonials` (+ `reviewer-names`), `moving-carriers` (+ `import`)
- **Booking recon:** `booking-lead-reconciliations/*`
- **Registry:** `operations-registry/{overview,health,changes}`
- **RingCentral:** `ringcentral/inbound-routes*`
- **Observability:** `observability/*` + exports
- **Google Drive:** `google-drive/*` (router file nested in `v1.routes.ts`)
- **Ingestion:** `ingestion/*` (separate `app.use` router)
- **Reporting:** `reporting/{catalog,destinations,definitions,draft,runs}` (separate `app.use` router)
- **Granot automation:** `granot-automation/runs/*`, `granot-automation/runs/sources`, `granot-automation/run-groups`, `granot-automation/runs/worker` (separate `app.use` router, before v1)
- **Granot lifecycle:** `granot-lifecycle/activation`, `granot-lifecycle/receipts/:id/requeue`, `granot-lifecycle/jobs/:normalized_job_no`, `granot-lifecycle/operations/health` (focused router mounted after the `/api/v1` guard)

`database_scope=production|historical|combined` where appropriate. Detail rejects `combined`; historical is read-only. No admin delete routes for core leads/bookings/customers — use public v1 writes so sheet sync stays owned by domain services. Observability deletes are the explicit exception.

Public v1 extras (still behind the v1 guard unless noted): `POST /api/v1/leadless-bookings`, `POST /api/v1/employee-booking-{options,submissions}` (secret + `x-public-client-key-hash` on submit), `POST /api/v1/form-leads/granot-match`, `/api/v1/granot-crm/csv/*`.

## Config Domain Modules (`src/config/domain/`)

`constants`, `sheets`, `sources`, `cpl` / `cplRateDefinitions`, `runtime`, `googleAuth`, `googleDriveOAuth`, `googlePicker`, `sheetSync`, `granotCsv`, `granotWebhook` (secret + env-scoped lifecycle queue topic/publish guard), `granotLifecycle` (ten processing/shadow/effect flags), `observability`, `leadMessaging`, `employeeBookingMatching`, `bookingReconciliation`, `reportingLiveTest` — barrel-exported via `domain.ts`.

**`reporting`** — delivery limits/flags; import `./domain/reporting` directly (not in barrel).

## Cross-Cutting Write Flow

Typical mutating path:

1. Validate (route Zod + service guards).
2. Persist Mongo (often transactional when sheet sync is involved).
3. Enqueue/schedule Google Sheet sync (`schedule*SheetSync`, `runSheetSyncWrite`, `persistSheetSyncIntent`).
4. Optionally CRM submit, customer upsert, CPL recompute/correction, lead messaging, observability events, or domain commands (ingest/automation).

Trace downstream targets before editing a write path.

## Script Launch Map

Run via `package.json` so `.env` + `tsx` stay consistent.

| Folder | Owns |
|--------|------|
| `scripts/dev_ops/` | Personal/admin DB ops, patches, Twilio, nested Google Sheets/Apps Script/Postman/RingCentral probes — treat as potentially destructive |
| `scripts/granot-automation/` | Local run + seed sources (`pnpm granot:*`) |
| `scripts/reporting/` | Live Google harness + artifact janitor (`pnpm reporting:*`) |
| `scripts/historical/` | Historical audits/backfills/repairs (+ relaxed historical models when present) |
| `scripts/historical_production_db_staged_merge_ingestion/` | Snapshot/plan/apply/verify/rollback (`pnpm historical:*`) |
| `scripts/migrations/` | Ops-registry seed/backfill/RC migrations (`pnpm migrations:*`) and Granot lifecycle receipt/source-registry/index migrations (`pnpm migration:granot-lifecycle:*`) |
| `scripts/prototypes/` | Granot lead-lifecycle prototype CLI (`pnpm prototype:granot-lifecycle`) — not runtime |
| `scripts/output/` | Generated artifacts (not runtime) |
| Root one-offs | `dev-server.ts`, `best-relocation-sheet-ingest.ts`, `generate-granot-webhook-secret.ts`, `test-setup.ts`, `dump-operations-name-link-inventory.ts` (`pnpm ops:dump-name-link-inventory`), `ingest-moving-carriers.ts` (`pnpm db:ingest-moving-carriers`), `test-create-google-spreadsheet.ts` |
| `scripts/dev_ops/twilio/`, `scripts/dev_ops/ping-db.ts` | `pnpm twilio:*`, `pnpm db:ping` |
| `scripts/dev_ops/ringcentral/` | Manual RC diagnostics/webhook runners — invoke with `tsx` + `.env`; **no** `pnpm ringcentral:*` scripts in `package.json` |

Keep reusable runtime logic in `src/services/`; scripts should call services, not reimplement them.

## Working Rules

- Preserve workflow boundaries: form/call/book/cancel/customer, sheet sync, RC ingest, extension enrich/recon/CSV, Granot webhooks (receipt capture + drain; no official Lead/Booking writes), Granot HTTP automation, ops registry, reporting, Best Relocation ingestion, employee booking/recon, lead messaging, historical work — separate concerns even when they share models.
- Prefer focused modules inside existing domain folders over growing `v1.routes.ts` or broad orchestration files.
- Mongo is source of truth; Sheets/CRM/S3/Twilio/Drive/reporting destinations are mode-aware side effects that need safe identifiers and logging.
- Registry/source/CPL/RC-route/ingestion/granot mutations need trusted owner actors when that gate already exists.
- After runtime TS changes: `pnpm test` and `pnpm typecheck` when practical.
